  "ears": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - THE EAR FLANGE IS BEHIND THE DUCT, NOT AT ITS ENDS. The 1U part's front view draws ear folds 23.1 mm in from each end and holes 464.47 apart; the 2U part's draws neither - the duct runs the full 482.59 - and its top view draws a plate across the whole width at the very rear, where the screws stand, with the base rails in front of it. The side view draws that plate 74.33 high behind the 84.33 finger walls. It is a different moulding, not the 1U part made taller: it bolts to the face of the rails through the ends of that plate and stands entirely in front of them, so `ears: behind`."
  },
  "fingers": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - the top view at 5.309 px/mm: seven straight fingers on a 48.5 mm pitch, the middle one on the middle of the duct, each two ribs 8.3 wide with a 9 mm slot between them, 25.4 across over the straight run and flaring to 28.4 at the rail, which is not drawn; and two flat walls at each end, from the end of the duct to 19.2 and from 40.5 to 60.1, drawn as one 19.4-wide part at 0 and 40.6. The gaps come out even, 23.1 between every pair. They are straight, where the 1U part's fingers have T-shaped tips. The hooked cable retainers the top view draws near the cover are not drawn. The top view shows one row; the bottom row is taken as the same, as the side view's two equal walls draw it."
