  "method": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "FIGURES FROM THE VENDOR DRAWING. The FS Horizontal Single Sided Manager datasheet (USCMH-SFDABSB1U and -B2U) has a specification table and, for the 2U part, a top view, a front view and a side view in millimetres on its third page, lettered CMH-SFDABSB2U. They are vector art, not embedded images, so the page was rendered at 600 dpi. The top view is 5.309 px/mm across its 482.59 and 5.41 down its 169.9 (Ref), a 2 per cent difference; the front view 5.379 across and 5.46 down its 88.81; the side view 3.436 along its 168.5 and 5.24 up its 84.33 and 74.33, which agree with each other - the side view is not to scale vertically, as on the 1U part. So widths come from the top and front views across, depths from the side view along, and heights from the dimensions and the side view's own vertical scale, never from one view's scale applied to another's axis. The part is portal-only: FS publishes no product page and no image of it, so there is no second reading."
  },
